{
  "schemaVersion": "1.0",
  "title": "Agentlas Global Commands",
  "type": "object",
  "required": [
    "schemaVersion",
    "packageId",
    "canonicalCommand",
    "commands",
    "postCreationUserMessage"
  ],
  "properties": {
    "schemaVersion": {
      "type": "string"
    },
    "packageId": {
      "type": "string"
    },
    "canonicalCommand": {
      "type": "string",
      "pattern": "^/[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]*(?::[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]*)?$"
    },
    "commands": {
      "type": "array",
      "minItems": 1,
      "description": "Command adapters this package exposes. Measured on the live corpus: 101 packages declare six, 68 declare exactly one, and the entry shape comes in four forms — the full {runtime, command, adapterPath, scope, status} record (100), {command, description, entry} (52), {name, entrypoint, description} (7), and that plus runtimeAdapters (4). The previous rule required four entries of the first form only, which made a package with one canonical command unpublishable forever. How many runtimes an author adapts to is their decision, not a schema constraint; the first form below stays the canonical one that generation writes.",
      "items": {
        "anyOf": [
          {
            "type": "object",
            "required": [
              "runtime",
              "command",
              "adapterPath",
              "scope",
              "status"
            ],
            "properties": {
              "runtime": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "command": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "adapterPath": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "globalInstallPath": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "scope": {
                "type": "string",
                "enum": [
                  "global",
                  "project",
                  "plugin",
                  "terminal"
                ]
              },
              "status": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "notes": {
                "type": "string"
              }
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "object",
            "required": [
              "command"
            ],
            "properties": {
              "command": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "description": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "entry": {
                "type": "string"
              }
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "object",
            "required": [
              "name"
            ],
            "properties": {
              "name": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "entrypoint": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "description": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "runtimeAdapters": {}
            }
          }
        ],
        "$comment": "anyOf, not oneOf. These are three ACCEPTED SHAPES, not mutually exclusive types: a full runtime-adapter entry also satisfies the minimal {command} shape, so oneOf rejected every complete entry with 'is valid under each of ...'. Measured 2026-08-17: 6 blockers per package on every generated package, including ones that were otherwise contract-complete. Adding additionalProperties:false instead would reject forward-compatible fields."
      }
    },
    "postCreationUserMessage": {
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "required",
        "template"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "required": {
          "type": "boolean"
        },
        "template": {
          "type": "string"
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
